msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: <Accordion>
# <AccordionItem title="Jawapan">
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(a) Since we are orthonormalizing the vectors as we produce them, a set of $N$ such vectors will form a complete basis, meaning a linear combination of them can be used to create any vector in the space.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(b) The orthogonalization process consists of subtracting off the projection of a new vector onto all previous vectors. If all previous vectors span the full vector space, then subtracting off projections onto the full subspace will always leave us with a zero vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"(a) Kerana kita mengortogonalkan vektor semasa kita menghasilkannya, satu set $N$ vektor sedemikian akan membentuk asas lengkap, bermakna gabungan linear mereka boleh digunakan untuk mencipta sebarang vektor dalam ruang tersebut.\n"
"(b) Proses pengortogonalan terdiri daripada menolak unjuran vektor baru ke atas semua vektor sebelumnya. Jika semua vektor sebelumnya merentangi ruang vektor penuh, maka menolak unjuran ke atas subruang penuh akan sentiasa menghasilkan vektor sifar.\n"

