# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Discussion and extension {#5-discussion-and-extension}"
msgstr "5. Perbincangan dan perluasan {#5-discussion-and-extension}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To recap, we start with a reference state, then evolve it for different periods of time to generate the unitary Krylov subspace. We project our Hamiltonian onto that subspace. We also estimate the overlaps of the subspace vectors. Finally we solve the lower-dimensional, generalized eigenvalue problem classically.\n"
msgstr "Untuk ringkasan, kita bermula dengan keadaan rujukan, kemudian mengevolusinya untuk tempoh masa yang berbeza untuk menjana subruang Krylov unitari. Kita mengunjurkan Hamiltonian kita ke atas subruang tersebut. Kita juga menganggar pertindihan vektor subruang. Akhirnya kita menyelesaikan masalah nilai eigen teritlak berdimensi lebih rendah secara klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A flow-chart overview of QKD: start with a reference state, evolve the state to approximate Krylov vectors, project into the Krylov subspace, diagonalize the projected subspace classically, and determine ground state properties.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/krylov/kqd-fig7.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran keseluruhan aliran kerja QKD: mulakan dengan keadaan rujukan, evolusikan keadaan untuk menganggar vektor Krylov, unjurkan ke subruang Krylov, diagonalisasikan subruang yang diunjurkan secara klasik, dan tentukan sifat keadaan tanah.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/krylov/kqd-fig7.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let’s compare what determines computational costs of using the Krylov technique classically and quantum mechanically. There are not perfect analogs between classical and quantum approaches for all steps. This table collects some scaling of different steps for consideration.\n"
msgstr "Mari kita bandingkan apa yang menentukan kos pengkomputeran menggunakan teknik Krylov secara klasik dan kuantum. Tiada analogi yang sempurna antara pendekatan klasik dan kuantum untuk semua langkah. Jadual ini mengumpulkan beberapa penskalaan langkah-langkah berbeza untuk pertimbangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A table describing scaling of different processes classically and in the quantum approach to Krylov methods. Some quantum steps have no analog. The scalings are the same as those stated in text.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/krylov/kqd-fig8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Jadual yang menerangkan penskalaan proses berbeza secara klasik dan dalam pendekatan kuantum kepada kaedah Krylov. Beberapa langkah kuantum tidak mempunyai analogi. Penskalaan adalah sama seperti yang dinyatakan dalam teks.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/krylov/kqd-fig8.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recall that Hamiltonians generally have terms that cannot be simultaneously measured (because they do not commute with on another). We sort terms in the Hamiltonian into groups of commuting Pauli operators that can all be measured simultaneously, and we may require many such groups to account for all the terms that do not commute with one another. To build up $\\tilde{H}$ on a quantum computer requires separate measurements for each group of commuting Pauli strings in the Hamiltonian, and each of those requires many shots. We must do this for $r^2$ different matrix elements, corresponding to $r^2$ combinations of different time evolution factors. There are sometimes ways to reduce this, but in this rough treatment, the time required for this scales like $N_\\text{shots}\\times N_\\text{GCP} \\times r^2.$ The elements of $S$ must be estimated, which scales like $O(N_\\text{shots}\\times r^2)$. Finally, solving the generalized eigenvalue problem in the projected space, classically, takes $O(r^3).$\n"
msgstr "Ingat bahawa Hamiltonian umumnya mempunyai sebutan yang tidak boleh diukur secara serentak (kerana ia tidak berkomut antara satu sama lain). Kita mengisih sebutan dalam Hamiltonian ke dalam kumpulan operator Pauli berkomut yang boleh semuanya diukur serentak, dan kita mungkin memerlukan banyak kumpulan sedemikian untuk merangkumi semua sebutan yang tidak berkomut antara satu sama lain. Untuk membina $\\tilde{H}$ pada komputer kuantum memerlukan pengukuran berasingan untuk setiap kumpulan rentetan Pauli berkomut dalam Hamiltonian, dan setiap satunya memerlukan banyak shots. Kita mesti melakukan ini untuk $r^2$ elemen matriks berbeza, sepadan dengan $r^2$ kombinasi faktor evolusi masa yang berbeza. Kadang-kadang terdapat cara untuk mengurangkan ini, tetapi dalam rawatan kasar ini, masa yang diperlukan untuk ini berskala seperti $N_\\text{shots}\\times N_\\text{GCP} \\times r^2.$ Elemen $S$ mesti dianggar, yang berskala seperti $O(N_\\text{shots}\\times r^2)$. Akhirnya, menyelesaikan masalah nilai eigen teritlak dalam ruang yang diunjurkan secara klasik mengambil $O(r^3).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that quantum Krylov diagonalization may be useful in cases where the number of commuting Pauli groups in the Hamiltonian is relatively small. These scaling dependencies suggest some applications where the Krylov method can be useful, and others where it likely will not be.\n"
"Some Hamiltonians have high complexity when mapped to qubits, involving many non-commuting Pauli strings that cannot easily be partitioned into a few commuting groups. This is often true of quantum chemistry problems, for example. This complexity presents two primary challenges for near-term quantum computers:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita melihat bahawa diagonalisasi krylov kuantum mungkin berguna dalam kes di mana bilangan kumpulan Pauli berkomut dalam Hamiltonian adalah agak kecil. Kebergantungan penskalaan ini mencadangkan beberapa aplikasi di mana kaedah Krylov boleh berguna, dan yang lain di mana ia mungkin tidak.\n"
"Beberapa Hamiltonian mempunyai kerumitan yang tinggi apabila dipetakan ke qubit, melibatkan banyak rentetan Pauli yang tidak berkomut yang tidak mudah dipartisi ke dalam beberapa kumpulan berkomut. Ini sering berlaku untuk masalah kimia kuantum, sebagai contoh. Kerumitan ini membentangkan dua cabaran utama untuk komputer kuantum jangka dekat:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The estimation of each element of $\\tilde{H}$ becomes computationally expensive due to the large number of terms.\n"
msgstr "Anggaran setiap elemen $\\tilde{H}$ menjadi mahal dari segi pengkomputeran disebabkan bilangan sebutan yang besar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The required Trotter circuits become prohibitively deep.\n"
msgstr "Litar Trotter yang diperlukan menjadi terlalu dalam.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both of the above points will be less problematic when quantum computers reach fault-tolerance, but they must be considered in the near term. Even systems with “simpler” mappings than those in quantum chemistry may experience the same impediments, if the Hamiltonians have too many non-commuting terms.\n"
"The Krylov method is most useful where the Hamiltonian can be partitioned into relatively few commuting Pauli groups, and where $H$ is easy to implement in trotter circuits. Both of these conditions are satisfied, for example, for many lattice models of interest in physics. KQD is especially useful if very little is known about the ground state. This stems from its inherent convergence guarantees and its applicability in scenarios where alternative methods are untenable due to insufficient ground state knowledge.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua-dua perkara di atas akan kurang bermasalah apabila komputer kuantum mencapai toleransi ralat, tetapi ia mesti dipertimbangkan dalam jangka dekat. Malah sistem dengan pemetaan yang lebih \"mudah\" daripada yang ada dalam kimia kuantum mungkin mengalami halangan yang sama, jika Hamiltonian mempunyai terlalu banyak sebutan yang tidak berkomut.\n"
"Kaedah Krylov paling berguna di mana Hamiltonian boleh dipartisi ke dalam beberapa kumpulan Pauli berkomut yang agak sedikit, dan di mana $H$ mudah dilaksanakan dalam litar Trotter. Kedua-dua syarat ini dipenuhi, sebagai contoh, untuk banyak model kekisi yang diminati dalam fizik. KQD sangat berguna jika sangat sedikit yang diketahui tentang keadaan tanah. Ini berpunca daripada jaminan konvergensi yang sedia ada dan kebolehgunaannya dalam senario di mana kaedah alternatif tidak boleh dilaksanakan kerana pengetahuan keadaan tanah yang tidak mencukupi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While KQD is a powerful tool, the protocol's time-consuming aspects, particularly the estimation of each element of the projected Hamiltonian and the overlap of Krylov states, represent opportunities for improvement. An alternative approach involves leveraging Krylov methods in conjunction with sampling-based methods, which are the subject of the next lesson.\n"
msgstr "Walaupun KQD adalah alat yang berkuasa, aspek-aspek protokol yang memakan masa, terutamanya anggaran setiap elemen Hamiltonian yang diunjurkan dan pertindihan keadaan Krylov, mewakili peluang untuk penambahbaikan. Pendekatan alternatif melibatkan memanfaatkan kaedah Krylov bersama kaedah berasaskan pensampelan, yang menjadi subjek pelajaran seterusnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Appendices {#6-appendices}"
msgstr "6. Lampiran {#6-appendices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix I: Krylov subspace from real time-evolutions {#appendix-i-krylov-subspace-from-real-time-evolutions}"
msgstr "Lampiran I: Subruang Krylov daripada evolusi masa nyata {#appendix-i-krylov-subspace-from-real-time-evolutions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The unitary Krylov space is defined as\n"
msgstr "Ruang Krylov unitari ditakrifkan sebagai\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U(H, |\\psi\\rangle) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ |\\psi\\rangle,  e^{-iH\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, \\dots, e^{-irH\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle \\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U(H, |\\psi\\rangle) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ |\\psi\\rangle,  e^{-iH\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, \\dots, e^{-irH\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle \\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for some timestep $dt$ that we will determine later. Temporarily assume $r$ is even: then define $d=r/2$. Notice that when we project the Hamiltonian into the Krylov space above, it is indistinguishable from the Krylov space\n"
msgstr "untuk beberapa langkah masa $dt$ yang akan kita tentukan kemudian. Buat sementara waktu andaikan $r$ adalah genap: kemudian definisikan $d=r/2$. Perhatikan bahawa apabila kita mengunjurkan Hamiltonian ke dalam ruang Krylov di atas, ia tidak dapat dibezakan daripada ruang Krylov\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U(H, |\\psi\\rangle) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ e^{i\\,d\\,H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle,  e^{i(d-1)H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, \\dots, e^{-i(d-1)H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, e^{-i\\,d\\,H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle \\right\\},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U(H, |\\psi\\rangle) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ e^{i\\,d\\,H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle,  e^{i(d-1)H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, \\dots, e^{-i(d-1)H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, e^{-i\\,d\\,H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle \\right\\},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"that is, where all the time-evolutions are shifted backward by $d$ timesteps.\n"
"The reason it is indistinguishable is because the matrix elements\n"
msgstr ""
"iaitu, di mana semua evolusi masa dianjak ke belakang sebanyak $d$ langkah masa.\n"
"Sebabnya tidak dapat dibezakan ialah elemen matriks\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{H}_{j,k} = \\langle\\psi|e^{i\\,j\\,H\\,dt}He^{-i\\,k\\,H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle=\\langle\\psi|He^{i(j-k)H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{H}_{j,k} = \\langle\\psi|e^{i\\,j\\,H\\,dt}He^{-i\\,k\\,H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle=\\langle\\psi|He^{i(j-k)H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "are invariant under overall shifts of the evolution time, since the time-evolutions commute with the Hamiltonian. For odd $r$, we can use the analysis for $r-1$.\n"
msgstr "tidak berubah di bawah anjakan keseluruhan masa evolusi, kerana evolusi masa berkomut dengan Hamiltonian. Untuk $r$ ganjil, kita boleh menggunakan analisis untuk $r-1$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We want to show that somewhere in this Krylov space, there is guaranteed to be a low-energy state. We do so by way of the following result, which is derived from Theorem 3.1 in [\\[3\\]](#references):\n"
msgstr "Kita ingin menunjukkan bahawa di suatu tempat dalam ruang Krylov ini, terdapat jaminan ada keadaan bertenaga rendah. Kita melakukan ini melalui keputusan berikut, yang diperoleh daripada Teorem 3.1 dalam [\\[3\\]](#references):\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Claim 1:** there exists a function $f$ such that for energies $E$ in the spectral range of the Hamiltonian (that is, between the ground state energy and the maximum energy)...\n"
msgstr "**Tuntutan 1:** terdapat fungsi $f$ sedemikian untuk tenaga $E$ dalam julat spektrum Hamiltonian (iaitu, antara tenaga keadaan tanah dan tenaga maksimum)...\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$f(E_0)=1$\n"
msgstr "$f(E_0)=1$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$|f(E)|\\le2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-d}$ for all values of $E$ that lie $\\ge\\delta$ away from $E_0$, that is, it is exponentially suppressed\n"
msgstr "$|f(E)|\\le2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-d}$ untuk semua nilai $E$ yang terletak $\\ge\\delta$ jauh daripada $E_0$, iaitu, ia ditekan secara eksponen\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$f(E)$ is a linear combination of $e^{ijE\\,dt}$ for $j=-d,-d+1,...,d-1,d$\n"
msgstr "$f(E)$ ialah gabungan linear $e^{ijE\\,dt}$ untuk $j=-d,-d+1,...,d-1,d$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We give a proof below, but that can be safely skipped unless one wants to understand the full, rigorous argument. For now we focus on the implications of the above claim. By property 3 above, we can see that the shifted Krylov space above contains the state $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$. This is our low-energy state. To see why, write $|\\psi\\rangle$ in the energy eigenbasis:\n"
msgstr "Kita berikan bukti di bawah, tetapi itu boleh dilangkau dengan selamat melainkan seseorang ingin memahami hujah penuh yang ketat. Buat masa ini kita fokus pada implikasi tuntutan di atas. Dengan sifat 3 di atas, kita dapat melihat bahawa ruang Krylov yang dianjak di atas mengandungi keadaan $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$. Inilah keadaan bertenaga rendah kita. Untuk melihat kenapa, tulis $|\\psi\\rangle$ dalam asas eigentenaga:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{k=0}^{N}\\gamma_k|E_k\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{k=0}^{N}\\gamma_k|E_k\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $|E_k\\rangle$ is the kth energy eigenstate and $\\gamma_k$ is its amplitude in the initial state $|\\psi\\rangle$. Expressed in terms of this, $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$ is given by\n"
msgstr "di mana $|E_k\\rangle$ ialah keadaan eigen tenaga ke-k dan $\\gamma_k$ ialah amplitudnya dalam keadaan awal $|\\psi\\rangle$. Dinyatakan dari segi ini, $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$ diberikan oleh\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"f(H)|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{k=0}^{N}\\gamma_kf(E_k)|E_k\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"f(H)|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{k=0}^{N}\\gamma_kf(E_k)|E_k\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "using the fact that we can replace $H$ by $E_k$ when it acts on the eigenstate $|E_k\\rangle$. The energy error of this state is therefore\n"
msgstr "menggunakan fakta bahawa kita boleh menggantikan $H$ dengan $E_k$ apabila ia bertindak pada keadaan eigen $|E_k\\rangle$. Ralat tenaga keadaan ini ialah\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} = \\frac{\\langle\\psi|f(H)(H-E_0)f(H)|\\psi\\rangle}{\\langle\\psi|f(H)^2|\\psi\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{ralat tenaga} = \\frac{\\langle\\psi|f(H)(H-E_0)f(H)|\\psi\\rangle}{\\langle\\psi|f(H)^2|\\psi\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"= \\frac{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"= \\frac{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To turn this into an upper bound that is easier to understand, we first separate the sum in the numerator into terms with $E_k-E_0\\le\\delta$ and terms with $E_k-E_0>\\delta$:\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengubah ini menjadi had atas yang lebih mudah difahami, kita mula-mula memisahkan jumlah dalam pengangka kepada sebutan dengan $E_k-E_0\\le\\delta$ dan sebutan dengan $E_k-E_0>\\delta$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} = \\frac{\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} + \\frac{\\sum_{E_k> E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{ralat tenaga} = \\frac{\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} + \\frac{\\sum_{E_k> E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can upper bound the first term by $\\delta$,\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh mengehadkan atas sebutan pertama dengan $\\delta$,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} < \\frac{\\delta\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} \\le \\delta,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} < \\frac{\\delta\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} \\le \\delta,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the first step follows because $E_k-E_0\\le\\delta$ for every $E_k$ in the sum, and the second step follows because the sum in the numerator is a subset of the sum in the denominator. For the second term, first we lower bound the denominator by $|\\gamma_0|^2$, since $f(E_0)^2=1$: adding everything back together, this gives\n"
msgstr "di mana langkah pertama mengikut kerana $E_k-E_0\\le\\delta$ untuk setiap $E_k$ dalam jumlah, dan langkah kedua mengikut kerana jumlah dalam pengangka adalah subset jumlah dalam penyebut. Untuk sebutan kedua, pertama kita mengehadkan bawah penyebut dengan $|\\gamma_0|^2$, kerana $f(E_0)^2=1$: menggabungkan semua kembali, ini memberikan\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} \\le \\delta + \\frac{1}{|\\gamma_0|^2}\\sum_{E_k>E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{ralat tenaga} \\le \\delta + \\frac{1}{|\\gamma_0|^2}\\sum_{E_k>E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To simplify what is left, notice that for all these $E_k$, by the definition of $f$ we know that $f(E_k)^2 \\le 4\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-2d}$. Additionally upper bounding $E_k-E_0<2\\|H\\|$ and upper bounding $\\sum_{E_k>E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2<1$ gives\n"
msgstr "Untuk memudahkan apa yang tinggal, perhatikan bahawa untuk semua $E_k$ ini, mengikut definisi $f$ kita tahu bahawa $f(E_k)^2 \\le 4\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-2d}$. Tambahan pula mengehadkan atas $E_k-E_0<2\\|H\\|$ dan mengehadkan atas $\\sum_{E_k>E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2<1$ memberikan\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} \\le \\delta + \\frac{8}{|\\gamma_0|^2}\\|H\\|\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-2d}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{ralat tenaga} \\le \\delta + \\frac{8}{|\\gamma_0|^2}\\|H\\|\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-2d}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This holds for any $\\delta>0$, so if we set $\\delta$ equal to our goal error, then the error bound above converges towards that exponentially with the Krylov dimension $2d=r$. Also note that if $\\delta<E_1-E_0$ then the $\\delta$ term actually goes away entirely in the above bound.\n"
msgstr "Ini berlaku untuk sebarang $\\delta>0$, jadi jika kita menetapkan $\\delta$ sama dengan ralat sasaran kita, maka had ralat di atas menumpu ke arah itu secara eksponen dengan dimensi Krylov $2d=r$. Juga perhatikan bahawa jika $\\delta<E_1-E_0$ maka sebutan $\\delta$ sebenarnya hilang sepenuhnya dalam had di atas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To complete the argument, we first note that the above is just the energy error of the particular state $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$, rather than the energy error of the lowest energy state in the Krylov space. However, by the (Rayleigh-Ritz) variational principle, the energy error of the lowest energy state in the Krylov space is upper bounded by the energy error of any state in the Krylov space, so the above is also an upper bound on the energy error of the lowest energy state, that is, the output of the Krylov quantum diagonalization algorithm.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melengkapkan hujah, kita perlu memperhatikan bahawa di atas hanyalah ralat tenaga keadaan tertentu $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$, bukan ralat tenaga keadaan bertenaga terendah dalam ruang Krylov. Namun, dengan prinsip variasi (Rayleigh-Ritz), ralat tenaga keadaan bertenaga terendah dalam ruang Krylov dibatasi oleh ralat tenaga mana-mana keadaan dalam ruang Krylov, jadi yang di atas juga merupakan had atas pada ralat tenaga keadaan bertenaga terendah, iaitu, output algoritma diagonalisasi krylov kuantum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A similar analysis as the above can be carried out that additionally accounts for noise and the thresholding procedure discussed in the notebook. See [\\[2\\]](#references) and [\\[4\\]](#references) for this analysis.\n"
msgstr "Analisis yang serupa seperti di atas boleh dijalankan yang juga mengambil kira hingar dan prosedur penghadan yang dibincangkan dalam buku nota. Lihat [\\[2\\]](#references) dan [\\[4\\]](#references) untuk analisis ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix II: proof of Claim 1 {#appendix-ii-proof-of-claim-1}"
msgstr "Lampiran II: Bukti Tuntutan 1 {#appendix-ii-proof-of-claim-1}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following is mostly derived from [\\[3\\]](#references), Theorem 3.1: let $0 < a < b$ and let $\\Pi^*_d$ be the space of residual polynomials (polynomials whose value at 0 is 1) of degree at most $d$. The solution to\n"
msgstr "Berikut ini kebanyakannya diperoleh daripada [\\[3\\]](#references), Teorem 3.1: biarkan $0 < a < b$ dan biarkan $\\Pi^*_d$ menjadi ruang polinomial residual (polinomial yang nilainya di 0 adalah 1) berdarjah paling tinggi $d$. Penyelesaian kepada\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\beta(a, b, d) = \\min_{p \\in \\Pi^*_d} \\max_{x \\in [a, b]} |p(x)| \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\beta(a, b, d) = \\min_{p \\in \\Pi^*_d} \\max_{x \\in [a, b]} |p(x)| \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is\n"
msgstr "ialah\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p^*(x) = \\frac{T_d\\left(\\frac{b + a - 2x}{b - a}\\right)}{T_d\\left(\\frac{b + a}{b - a}\\right)}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p^*(x) = \\frac{T_d\\left(\\frac{b + a - 2x}{b - a}\\right)}{T_d\\left(\\frac{b + a}{b - a}\\right)}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and the corresponding minimal value is\n"
msgstr "dan nilai minimum yang bersamaan ialah\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\beta(a, b, d) = T_d^{-1}\\left(\\frac{b + a}{b - a}\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\beta(a, b, d) = T_d^{-1}\\left(\\frac{b + a}{b - a}\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We want to convert this into a function that can be expressed naturally in terms of complex exponentials, because those are the real time-evolutions that generate the quantum Krylov space.\n"
"To do so, it is convenient to introduce the following transformation of energies within the spectral range of the Hamiltonian to numbers in the range $[0,1]$: define\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita ingin menukar ini kepada fungsi yang boleh dinyatakan secara semula jadi dalam sebutan eksponen kompleks, kerana itulah evolusi masa nyata yang menjana ruang Krylov kuantum.\n"
"Untuk melakukan ini, adalah mudah untuk memperkenalkan transformasi tenaga dalam julat spektrum Hamiltonian kepada nombor dalam julat $[0,1]$ berikut: takrifkan\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"g(E) = \\frac{1-\\cos\\big((E-E_0)dt\\big)}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"g(E) = \\frac{1-\\cos\\big((E-E_0)dt\\big)}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $dt$ is a timestep such that $-\\pi < E_0dt < E_\\text{max}dt < \\pi$.\n"
"Notice that $g(E_0)=0$ and $g(E)$ grows as $E$ moves away from $E_0$.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $dt$ ialah langkah masa sedemikian sehingga $-\\pi < E_0dt < E_\\text{max}dt < \\pi$.\n"
"Perhatikan bahawa $g(E_0)=0$ dan $g(E)$ berkembang apabila $E$ bergerak jauh dari $E_0$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now using the polynomial $p^*(x)$ with the parameters a, b, d set to $a = g(E_0 + \\delta)$, $b = 1$, and d = int(r/2), we define the function:\n"
msgstr "Sekarang menggunakan polinomial $p^*(x)$ dengan parameter a, b, d ditetapkan kepada $a = g(E_0 + \\delta)$, $b = 1$, dan d = int(r/2), kita mendefinisikan fungsi:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"f(E) = p^* \\left( g(E) \\right) = \\frac{T_d\\left(1 + 2\\frac{\\cos\\big((E-E_0)dt\\big) - \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 +\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)}{T_d\\left(1 + 2\\frac{1-\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 + \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"f(E) = p^* \\left( g(E) \\right) = \\frac{T_d\\left(1 + 2\\frac{\\cos\\big((E-E_0)dt\\big) - \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 +\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)}{T_d\\left(1 + 2\\frac{1-\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 + \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $E_0$ is the ground state energy. We can see by inserting $\\cos(x)=\\frac{e^{ix}+e^{-ix}}{2}$ that $f(E)$ is a trigonometric polynomial of degree $d$, that is, a linear combination of $e^{ijE\\,dt}$ for $j=-d,-d+1,...,d-1,d$. Furthermore, from the definition of $p^*(x)$ above we have that $f(E_0)=p(0)=1$ and for any $E$ in the spectral range such that $\\vert E-E_0 \\vert > \\delta$ we have\n"
msgstr "di mana $E_0$ ialah tenaga keadaan tanah. Kita dapat melihat dengan menyisipkan $\\cos(x)=\\frac{e^{ix}+e^{-ix}}{2}$ bahawa $f(E)$ ialah polinomial trigonometri berdarjah $d$, iaitu, gabungan linear $e^{ijE\\,dt}$ untuk $j=-d,-d+1,...,d-1,d$. Tambahan pula, daripada definisi $p^*(x)$ di atas kita ada bahawa $f(E_0)=p(0)=1$ dan untuk sebarang $E$ dalam julat spektrum sedemikian sehingga $\\vert E-E_0 \\vert > \\delta$ kita ada\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|f(E)| \\le \\beta(a, b, d) = T_d^{-1}\\left(1 + 2\\frac{1-\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 + \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|f(E)| \\le \\beta(a, b, d) = T_d^{-1}\\left(1 + 2\\frac{1-\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 + \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\leq 2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-d} = 2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-\\lfloor k/2\\rfloor}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\leq 2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-d} = 2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-\\lfloor k/2\\rfloor}.\n"
"$$\n"

